Pre-orders of Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> may not open until Saturday, September 12, a day later than the company's usual schedule, according to a new report.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/iPhone-18-Pro-Dark-Cherry-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059225" /><br/>
Apple is set to hold its <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/26/apple-iphone-event-2026/">annual iPhone event</a> on Wednesday, September 9, where the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; models, its first-ever foldable iPhone, and the Apple Watch Series 12 and Ultra 4 are all expected to be announced. <br/>
<br/>
Under Apple's typical launch plan, pre-orders begin the Friday immediately following the event, with devices shipping the following Friday. This year, that would place pre-orders on Friday, September 11, but <a href="https://www.macworld.com/article/3222711/iphone-18-pro-pre-orders-later-than-usual.html"><em>Macworld</em></a> reports that its German sister publication, <a href="https://www.macwelt.de/"><em>Macwelt</em></a>, has heard from a reliable source that Apple will instead push pre-orders back to Saturday, September 12.<br/>
<br/>
There is precedent for this as the shift is reportedly tied to the date itself. September 11, 2026 marks the 25th anniversary of the September 11 attacks, and Apple has moved pre-orders away from that date before. In 2015, when the standard pre-order Friday also landed on September 11, Apple delayed iPhone 6S and 6S Plus pre-orders to Saturday, September 12.<br/>
<br/>
The timing within the day is also said to be changing. Apple's pre-orders traditionally open at 5 a.m. PT, but the source says this year's window will instead start at midnight PT on Saturday.<br/>
<br/>
The delayed pre-order date is expected to apply to the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj;, Apple Watch Series 12, and Apple Watch Ultra 4, alongside any other hardware Apple introduces at the event. Apple's foldable iPhone could follow at a later date, with pre-orders potentially not opening until late September.<br/>
<br/>
